/* Waterdrop Survivor
   ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   GENRE, corrected by Timmy 2026-08-17 — this header used to say "Dead
   Cells inspired", which was misleading enough to steer design decisions
   the wrong way. What it actually is:

     Survivor · roguelite · bullet-hell · RPG
     Closest references: VAMPIRE SURVIVORS and HALLS OF TORMENT.

   TWO PROGRESSION LOOPS, and they are not the same thing. Do not conflate
   them when balancing or building UI:

     1. INSIDE a run — TEMPORARY. XP, level-ups, level-up cards, weapon
        evolutions, in-run builds. ALL OF IT RESETS the moment the run
        ends: death, completion, or quit. This is the roguelike part, and
        the only thing the Dead Cells comparison ever referred to.

     2. BETWEEN runs — PERMANENT, and THE POINT OF THE GAME. What you
        carry out of a run is resources, and you spend them in camp:
        meta upgrades, skill tree, talents, gear, abilities. These are
        kept forever and are what let you START the next run or map
        stronger than you started the last one.

   Loop 2 is not a slow background layer. A run is how you EARN permanent
   power; the permanent power is why the next run reaches further. Both
   loops must feel good, but only loop 2 is progress the player keeps.

   The "minigames" are NOT minigames. Each is meant to be as large as the
   main mode, just a different genre — its own levels, rarity, weapons and
   equipment, and roguelite progression of its own. Variation, not filler.
   ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
/* ══ LOCAL FONT FAMILIES ════════════════════════════════════════════
   Timmy dropped ~50 font files into the project; they live in
   `public/fonts/`. VT323 / Cinzel / JetBrains Mono still come from Google
   Fonts via the <link> in public/index.html — these are the local ones.

   TWO RULES, and they exist so a font swap later is one line and not a hunt
   through twenty files:
     1. Declare each family here ONCE, with font-display: swap.
     2. Screens reference a --font-* CUSTOM PROPERTY, never the family name
        inline. Renaming or replacing a family then touches only this block.
   ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */
/* Fonts referenced from CSS must live under src/, not public/. A root-relative
   `url('/fonts/…')` is resolved by css-loader as a module request and fails the
   build outright ("Can't resolve '/fonts/…' in 'src'"). Importing from src also
   gets the file hashed and cache-busted, which the public/ copy would not.
   `public/fonts/` still holds all ~50 originals plus the throwaway
   fontspec.html specimen page; copy a family in here as it gets wired up. */
@font-face {
  font-family: 'Velodrome Stencil';
  src: url('./fonts/VelodromeFuturisticTechStencil-Yq6wL.ttf') format('truetype');
  font-weight: 400;
  font-display: swap;
}
@font-face {
  font-family: 'Dragon Knight';
  src: url('./fonts/DragonKnight-xRDg0.otf') format('opentype');
  font-weight: 400;
  font-display: swap;
}
@font-face {
  font-family: 'Brandal Legend';
  src: url('./fonts/BrandalLegendDemo-ovDWo.ttf') format('truetype');
  font-weight: 400;
  font-display: swap;
}
@font-face {
  font-family: 'Keygen';
  src: url('./fonts/Keygen-BLAj3.otf') format('opentype');
  font-weight: 400;
  font-display: swap;
}
@font-face {
  font-family: 'Quwen King';
  src: url('./fonts/QuwenKingRegular-2OPEK.ttf') format('truetype');
  font-weight: 400;
  font-display: swap;
}
@font-face {
  font-family: 'Pixel Coleco';
  src: url('./fonts/PixelColeco-4vJW.ttf') format('truetype');
  font-weight: 400;
  font-display: swap;
}

:root {
  /* Machined hardware: engraved plate marks, instrument housings. */
  --font-hardware: 'Velodrome Stencil', 'VT323', monospace;
  --font-epic: 'Dragon Knight', 'Cinzel', serif;
  --font-legend: 'Brandal Legend', 'Cinzel', serif;
  --font-tech: 'Keygen', 'Velodrome Stencil', monospace;
  --font-card: 'Quwen King', 'Cinzel', serif;
  --font-pixel: 'Pixel Coleco', 'VT323', monospace;

  --bg-0: #07060c;
  --bg-1: #100a1a;
  --bg-2: #1a1226;
  --ink: #e8e0d2;
  --ink-dim: #9a8fa6;
  --accent: #ff7a1a;        /* ember orange — the primary UI accent */
  --accent-2: #ffd166;      /* gold */
  --blood: #b51d28;
  --water: #4dc4ff;
  --eldritch: #b362ff;
  --eldritch-dim: #6b3aa6;
  --rune: #4dffd4;
  --shadow: 0 0 0 1px #000, 0 0 0 2px #ffffff14, 0 12px 30px #000a;
  --pixel-edge: 0 0 0 2px #000, inset 0 0 0 1px #ffffff14;
}

* { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
html, body, #root {
  width: 100%;
  min-height: 100%;
  background: var(--bg-0);
  color: var(--ink);
  font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
  -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
  user-select: none;
}
html, body { cursor: default; }
body.in-game { cursor: crosshair; }
body {
  image-rendering: pixelated;
  overflow-x: hidden;
  overflow-y: auto;
  -webkit-overflow-scrolling: touch;
  overscroll-behavior: contain;
  touch-action: manipulation;
}
/* When in-game, lock scroll. App.js sets this class on body */
body.in-game {
  overflow: hidden;
  position: fixed;
  inset: 0;
}

/* Animated background grain */
body::before {
  content: '';
  position: fixed; inset: 0;
  background:
    radial-gradient(ellipse at 20% 10%, #2a0f4280 0%, transparent 50%),
    radial-gradient(ellipse at 80% 90%, #0f2a4280 0%, transparent 50%),
    repeating-linear-gradient(0deg, #0000 0 2px, #ffffff05 2px 3px);
  pointer-events: none;
  z-index: 0;
}

button {
  font-family: 'Cinzel', serif;
  font-weight: 800;
  letter-spacing: 0.12em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--ink);
  background: linear-gradient(180deg, #1c1228, #0e0816);
  border: 2px solid #000;
  box-shadow: var(--pixel-edge), 0 6px 0 #000;
  padding: 14px 26px;
  cursor: pointer;
  position: relative;
  transition: transform 80ms, box-shadow 80ms, color 120ms, background 120ms;
  overflow: visible;
}
button::after {
  content: '';
  position: absolute; inset: 0;
  background: linear-gradient(120deg, transparent 30%, rgba(255,255,255,0.06) 50%, transparent 70%);
  transform: translateX(-100%);
  transition: transform 400ms ease;
}
button:hover::after { transform: translateX(100%); }
button:hover {
  color: var(--accent-2);
  transform: translateY(-2px);
  box-shadow: var(--pixel-edge), 0 8px 0 #000, 0 0 30px #ff7a1a55;
  background: linear-gradient(180deg, #261a38, #0e0816);
}
button:active { transform: translateY(2px) scale(0.97); box-shadow: var(--pixel-edge), 0 2px 0 #000, 0 0 22px var(--accent-2, #ff7a1a); filter: brightness(1.35); }
button:disabled { opacity: 0.45; cursor: not-allowed; }

h1, h2, h3 { font-family: 'Cinzel', serif; letter-spacing: 0.08em; }

.app-shell {
  position: relative;
  min-height: 100vh;
  width: 100%;
  display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
  z-index: 1;
  padding: 16px;
}

/* MENU */
.menu {
  width: min(720px, 92vw);
  padding: 38px 42px;
  background:
    linear-gradient(180deg, #1a0f2a 0%, #0a0612 100%);
  border: 2px solid #000;
  box-shadow: 0 0 0 2px #ff7a1a44, 0 30px 80px #000c;
  text-align: center;
  position: relative;
}
.menu::before {
  content: '';
  position: absolute; inset: 8px;
  border: 1px dashed #ff7a1a55;
  pointer-events: none;
}
.title {
  font-size: clamp(40px, 7vw, 78px);
  background: linear-gradient(180deg, #ffd166, #ff7a1a 60%, #b51d28);
  -webkit-background-clip: text; background-clip: text;
  color: transparent;
  text-shadow: 0 0 30px #ff7a1a55;
  margin-bottom: 4px;
}
.subtitle {
  font-family: 'VT323', monospace;
  color: var(--rune);
  font-size: 22px;
  letter-spacing: 0.4em;
  margin-bottom: 28px;
  text-shadow: 0 0 14px #4dffd455;
}
.tagline {
  color: var(--ink-dim);
  font-family: 'VT323', monospace;
  font-size: 18px;
  margin-bottom: 28px;
  letter-spacing: 0.1em;
}
.menu-footer {
  margin-top: 24px;
  font-family: 'VT323', monospace;
  color: var(--ink-dim);
  font-size: 14px;
  letter-spacing: 0.2em;
}

/* GAME CANVAS */
.game-stage {
  position: fixed; inset: 0;
  background: #000;
  z-index: 1;
}
canvas#game, canvas.starraid-canvas {
  position: absolute; inset: 0;
  width: 100%; height: 100%;
  display: block;
  image-rendering: pixelated;
}

/* HUD */
.hud-top {
  position: absolute; top: 14px; left: 0; right: 0;
  display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; gap: 6px;
  pointer-events: none; z-index: 3;
  text-shadow: 0 2px 0 #000;
}
.hud-timer {
  font-family: 'Cinzel', serif; font-weight: 800;
  font-size: 36px; color: var(--ink);
  letter-spacing: 0.18em;
}
.hud-wave { color: var(--accent-2); font-family: 'VT323', monospace; font-size: 18px; letter-spacing: 0.3em; }
.hud-xpbar {
  width: min(680px, 70vw); height: 10px;
  background: #00000099;
  border: 1px solid #000;
  box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px #ffffff22;
  position: relative; overflow: hidden;
}
.hud-hp-text {
  position: absolute; right: 8px; top: -3px;
  font-family: 'VT323', monospace; font-size: 16px;
  color: var(--rune);
}

.hud-bottom {
  position: absolute; bottom: 14px; left: 14px; right: 14px;
  display: flex; align-items: flex-end; justify-content: space-between;
  pointer-events: none; z-index: 3;
}
.hud-hp {
  width: 280px;
}
.hud-hp-bar {
  height: 22px;
  background: #00000099;
  border: 2px solid #000;
  box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px #ffffff22, 0 0 0 1px #b51d2844;
  position: relative;
}
.hud-hp-fill {
  height: 100%;
  background: linear-gradient(90deg, #ff3146, #b51d28);
  box-shadow: 0 0 12px #b51d2888;
  transition: width 150ms ease-out;
  position: relative;
  overflow: hidden;
}
.hud-hp-fill.low {
  background: linear-gradient(90deg, #ff0000, #8b0000);
  animation: hpBarPulse 0.7s ease-in-out infinite;
}
.hud-hp-fill::after {
  content: '';
  position: absolute; top: 0; left: -100%; width: 50%; height: 100%;
  background: linear-gradient(90deg, transparent, rgba(255,255,255,0.2), transparent);
  animation: shine 2.5s ease-in-out infinite;
}
.hud-xpbar-fill {
  height: 100%;
  background: linear-gradient(90deg, #4dffd4, #4dc4ff, #b362ff);
  box-shadow: 0 0 12px #4dffd488;
  transition: width 300ms cubic-bezier(0.34,1.56,0.64,1);
  position: relative;
}
.hud-xpbar-fill::after {
  content: '';
  position: absolute; top: 0; left: -100%; width: 50%; height: 100%;
  background: linear-gradient(90deg, transparent, rgba(255,255,255,0.25), transparent);
  animation: shine 1.8s ease-in-out infinite;
}
.hud-hp-text {
  position: absolute; inset: 0;
  display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
  font-family: 'VT323', monospace; font-size: 18px;
  color: #fff; text-shadow: 0 1px 0 #000, 0 0 6px #000;
}
.hud-level {
  position: absolute; right: 8px; top: -3px;
  font-family: 'VT323', monospace; font-size: 16px;
  color: var(--rune);
}
.hud-stats {
  display: flex; gap: 18px;
  font-family: 'VT323', monospace;
  font-size: 20px;
  color: var(--ink);
  text-shadow: 0 2px 0 #000;
}
.hud-stat { display: flex; gap: 6px; align-items: center; }
.hud-stat .lbl { color: var(--ink-dim); font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: 0.2em; }
.hud-stat .val { color: var(--accent-2); }

.weapon-strip {
  position: absolute; top: 90px; left: 16px; transform: none;
  display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-start; gap: 6px;
  pointer-events: none; z-index: 3;
}
.weapon-strip > .weapon-chip-row {
  display: flex; gap: 8px;
}
/* Passive icons strip — small row under weapons */
.passive-strip {
  display: flex; gap: 4px; flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: flex-start; max-width: 320px;
}
.passive-chip {
  width: 28px; height: 28px;
  background: #0a061299;
  border: 1px solid #ffffff22;
  display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
  font-size: 14px;
  border-radius: 2px;
}
.weapon-chip {
  width: 56px; height: 56px;
  background: #0a0612cc;
  border: 2px solid #000;
  box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px #ffffff22, 0 0 14px #0008;
  display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
  position: relative;
  font-family: 'VT323', monospace;
  font-size: 26px;
  color: var(--ink);
}
.weapon-chip .lv {
  position: absolute; bottom: -2px; right: -2px;
  background: #000;
  color: var(--accent-2);
  font-size: 12px; padding: 1px 4px;
  border: 1px solid #ffd16688;
}

/* LEVEL UP MODAL */
.modal-overlay {
  position: fixed; inset: 0;
  background: radial-gradient(ellipse at center, #1a0f2acc 0%, #000d 70%);
  display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
  z-index: 10;
  backdrop-filter: blur(2px);
  animation: fadeIn 200ms;
  overflow-y: auto;
  padding: 20px;
  -webkit-overflow-scrolling: touch;
}
@keyframes fadeIn { from { opacity: 0; } to { opacity: 1; } }

/* ═══ DOPAMINE ANIMATIONS ═════════════════════════════════════ */
@keyframes claimBurst {
  0%   { transform: scale(1); box-shadow: var(--pixel-edge), 0 6px 0 #000; filter: brightness(1); }
  20%  { transform: scale(1.18) rotate(-1.5deg); box-shadow: var(--pixel-edge), 0 8px 0 #000, 0 0 40px #ffd16699, 0 0 80px #4dffd433; filter: brightness(1.6); }
  40%  { transform: scale(1.12) rotate(1deg); }
  60%  { transform: scale(1.06); box-shadow: var(--pixel-edge), 0 8px 0 #000, 0 0 20px #ff7a1a55; }
  100% { transform: scale(1); box-shadow: var(--pixel-edge), 0 6px 0 #000; filter: brightness(1); }
}
.claim-burst { animation: claimBurst 0.55s cubic-bezier(0.34,1.56,0.64,1) forwards; }

@keyframes rewardPop {
  0%   { transform: scale(0.5) translateY(20px); opacity: 0; }
  60%  { transform: scale(1.12) translateY(-4px); opacity: 1; }
  80%  { transform: scale(0.97) translateY(0); }
  100% { transform: scale(1) translateY(0); opacity: 1; }
}
.reward-pop { animation: rewardPop 0.45s cubic-bezier(0.34,1.56,0.64,1) both; }

@keyframes goldFloat {
  0%   { transform: translateY(0) scale(1); opacity: 1; }
  100% { transform: translateY(-32px) scale(1.3); opacity: 0; }
}
.gold-float { animation: goldFloat 0.9s ease-out forwards; pointer-events: none; }

@keyframes tabPing {
  0%   { transform: scale(1); }
  40%  { transform: scale(1.22); filter: drop-shadow(0 0 6px var(--rune)); }
  100% { transform: scale(1); }
}
.tab-ping { animation: tabPing 0.6s ease both; }

@keyframes levelUpShine {
  0%   { background-position: -200% center; }
  100% { background-position: 200% center; }
}

@keyframes questDone {
  0%   { box-shadow: var(--pixel-edge); }
  50%  { box-shadow: var(--pixel-edge), 0 0 0 3px #4dffd4, 0 0 24px #4dffd455; }
  100% { box-shadow: var(--pixel-edge), 0 0 0 2px #4dffd4aa; }
}
.quest-row.done { animation: questDone 0.8s ease forwards; border-color: var(--rune); }

@keyframes hpBarPulse {
  0%,100% { filter: brightness(1); }
  50%      { filter: brightness(1.35) drop-shadow(0 0 4px #ff3146); }
}

/* ─── Level Up Screen — title uses original definition at line ~1022 ─── */
@keyframes cardPop {
  0%   { transform: scale(1); box-shadow: var(--pixel-edge), 0 4px 0 #000; }
  30%  { transform: scale(1.10) rotate(-1.5deg); box-shadow: var(--pixel-edge), 0 4px 0 #000, 0 0 28px #ff7a1a99; }
  60%  { transform: scale(1.07) rotate(1deg); box-shadow: var(--pixel-edge), 0 4px 0 #000, 0 0 20px #ffd16699; }
  100% { transform: scale(1); box-shadow: var(--pixel-edge), 0 4px 0 #000; }
}
.card-pop { animation: cardPop 0.5s cubic-bezier(0.34,1.56,0.64,1); }
/* Cards deal in on an arc rather than sliding straight up: they start
   tipped away and rotate flat as they land, which is what sells them as
   physical cards on a table instead of rectangles fading in. */
@keyframes cardIn {
  0%   { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(56px) rotateX(48deg) scale(0.86); }
  60%  { opacity: 1; transform: translateY(-6px) rotateX(-7deg) scale(1.03); }
  100% { opacity: 1; transform: translateY(0) rotateX(0deg) scale(1); }
}
.levelup {
  display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center;
  gap: 22px;
}
@keyframes pulse {
  0%,100% { transform: scale(1); }
  50% { transform: scale(1.04); }
}
.levelup-sub {
  font-family: 'VT323', monospace;
  color: var(--ink-dim);
  letter-spacing: 0.3em;
  font-size: 18px;
}
/* Shared perspective on the row so every card tips around the same vanishing
   point — perspective set per-card would give each one its own, and the
   deal-in would look like independent flat rotations. */
.card-row {
  display: flex; gap: 18px; flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: center;
  max-width: 1100px; width: 100%;
  perspective: 1400px;
  perspective-origin: 50% 30%;
}
/* Daily lucky spin wheel — simple radial slice layout + spin animation. */
/* ── Daily spin wheel ────────────────────────────────────────────
   The face is rotated to a computed angle so the pointer lands on the
   slice that was actually rolled (see Welcome.jsx doSpin) — the old wheel
   span a fixed 1080deg and announced an unrelated prize, which is why the
   result never matched where it stopped. */
.spin-stage {
  position: relative; width: 190px; height: 190px; margin: 10px auto 4px;
  perspective: 620px;
}
.spin-pointer {
  position: absolute; top: -4px; left: 50%; transform: translateX(-50%);
  width: 0; height: 0; z-index: 4;
  border-left: 11px solid transparent;
  border-right: 11px solid transparent;
  border-top: 20px solid #ffd166;
  filter: drop-shadow(0 2px 5px rgba(0,0,0,0.8)) drop-shadow(0 0 7px #ffd16699);
}
/* Tilted rim gives the wheel real dimension instead of a flat disc. */
.spin-wheel-rim {
  position: absolute; inset: 0;
  border-radius: 50%;
  transform: rotateX(24deg);
  transform-style: preserve-3d;
  border: 5px solid #c8912f;
  background: conic-gradient(from 0deg, #7a5518, #ffe9a8 12%, #a8762a 27%, #ffe9a8 46%, #7a5518 62%, #ffd98a 80%, #7a5518 100%);
  box-shadow:
    0 14px 26px rgba(0,0,0,0.65),
    inset 0 0 0 3px rgba(0,0,0,0.55),
    0 0 26px rgba(255,209,102,0.30);
}
.spin-lamp {
  position: absolute; top: 50%; left: 50%;
  width: 5px; height: 5px; margin: -2.5px 0 0 -2.5px;
  border-radius: 50%;
  background: #6a5320;
  transform-origin: 50% 50%;
  box-shadow: 0 0 3px rgba(0,0,0,0.6);
  /* the inline transform is rotate(angle) translateY(-92px) — rotate first,
     then push out to the rim */
}
.spin-lamp.lit { animation: spinLamp 0.42s linear infinite; }
@keyframes spinLamp {
  0%, 100% { background: #6a5320; box-shadow: 0 0 3px rgba(0,0,0,0.6); }
  50%      { background: #fff3c4; box-shadow: 0 0 8px #ffd166; }
}
.spin-wheel-face {
  position: absolute; inset: 7px;
  border-radius: 50%;
  overflow: hidden;
  box-shadow: inset 0 0 22px rgba(0,0,0,0.85), inset 0 6px 14px rgba(255,255,255,0.06);
  /* Long, heavy ease-out so it decelerates like a real wheel. Duration
     must stay in sync with the award timeout in doSpin. */
  transition: transform 3.2s cubic-bezier(.12,.72,.12,1);
  will-change: transform;
}
.spin-spoke {
  position: absolute; top: 50%; left: 50%;
  width: 1px; height: 50%;
  background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(255,255,255,0.22), rgba(255,255,255,0.02));
  transform-origin: 50% 0;
}
/* Each slice is a full-size box rotated about the wheel centre, with its
   content pinned to the top edge so the rotation carries it around the rim.
   align-items MUST be flex-start: with the default `stretch` the inner
   element becomes full height, so its own transform-origin lands on the
   wheel centre and the counter-rotation that keeps the label upright
   instead undoes the slice rotation entirely — which is what stacked every
   icon on top of each other at 12 o'clock. */
.spin-slice {
  position: absolute; inset: 0;
  display: flex; justify-content: center; align-items: flex-start;
  pointer-events: none;
}
.spin-slice-inner {
  display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; gap: 1px;
  margin-top: 13px;
  transform-origin: 50% 50%;
}
.spin-slice-icon { font-size: 19px; filter: drop-shadow(0 1px 3px #000); line-height: 1; }
.spin-slice-inner .game-icon { filter: drop-shadow(0 1px 3px rgba(0,0,0,0.9)); }
.spin-result-icon .game-icon { filter: drop-shadow(0 0 8px currentColor); }
.spin-slice-amt {
  font-family: 'VT323', monospace; font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: 0.04em;
  color: rgba(255,255,255,0.72); text-shadow: 0 1px 2px #000;
}
.spin-slice.jackpot .spin-slice-icon { filter: drop-shadow(0 0 6px #ffd166); }
.spin-slice.jackpot .spin-slice-amt { color: #ffd166; }
/* Only filter is animated here — the element already carries a counter-
   rotation in its inline transform, so touching transform would undo it. */
.spin-slice.won .spin-slice-inner { animation: spinWon 0.5s ease-out 3 both; }
@keyframes spinWon {
  0%, 100% { filter: none; }
  50%      { filter: brightness(1.9) drop-shadow(0 0 10px #ffd166); }
}
.spin-wheel-hub {
  position: absolute; top: 50%; left: 50%; transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
  width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 50%;
  background: radial-gradient(circle at 38% 30%, #3a2c12 0%, #0a0612 75%);
  border: 3px solid #c8912f;
  display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
  font-size: 17px; z-index: 3;
  box-shadow: 0 4px 10px rgba(0,0,0,0.7), 0 0 14px rgba(255,209,102,0.45), inset 0 2px 5px rgba(255,255,255,0.12);
}
.spin-result {
  margin-top: 10px;
  display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; gap: 9px;
  font-family: 'VT323', monospace;
  color: #ffd166; font-size: 16px; letter-spacing: 0.05em;
  padding: 7px 10px;
  border: 1px solid #ffd16644;
  background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(255,209,102,0.12), rgba(255,209,102,0.02));
  animation: spinResultIn 0.45s cubic-bezier(.2,.9,.3,1.5) both;
}
.spin-result-icon { font-size: 22px; filter: drop-shadow(0 0 6px currentColor); }
.spin-result.jackpot {
  color: #fff3c4;
  border-color: #ffd166;
  box-shadow: 0 0 24px rgba(255,209,102,0.5), inset 0 0 18px rgba(255,209,102,0.15);
}
@keyframes spinResultIn {
  from { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(10px) scale(0.9); }
  to   { opacity: 1; transform: none; }
}

/* Tier escalation banner — big center-screen callout, fires once per boss kill. */
.tier-banner {
  position: fixed; top: 22%; left: 50%; transform: translateX(-50%);
  text-align: center; z-index: 2200; pointer-events: none;
  animation: tierBannerIn 0.5s cubic-bezier(.2,.9,.3,1.4) both;
}
.tier-banner-num {
  font-family: 'Cinzel', serif; font-weight: 900; letter-spacing: 0.12em;
  font-size: clamp(36px, 7vw, 64px); color: #ff3146;
  text-shadow: 0 0 20px #ff3146, 0 0 44px rgba(255,49,70,0.6), 0 4px 0 #000;
}
.tier-banner-sub {
  font-family: 'VT323', monospace; font-size: clamp(14px, 2.4vw, 20px);
  letter-spacing: 0.1em; color: #ffd166; margin-top: 4px;
  text-shadow: 0 0 10px #ffd16688, 0 2px 0 #000;
}
@keyframes tierBannerIn { from { transform: translateX(-50%) scale(0.7); } to { transform: translateX(-50%) scale(1); } }

/* Camp menu unlock reveal — fires when a base-building purchase cracks open
   a new batch of camp tabs (see Camp.jsx's unlockQueue). Timmy asked for
   exactly this kind of "dopamine" beat: big, dead center, one menu's icon
   blown up and swung in at a time, so each unlock gets its own moment
   instead of a wall of text. */
/* ── UNLOCKED reveal ────────────────────────────────────────────────
   This fires the handful of times a save opens a whole new part of the
   game, so it should read as an EVENT, not a toast. Every part is
   STAGGERED — rays, rings, logo, word, name — because the previous
   version scaled the lot in together and landed as one flat pop.
   Held longer too (1800ms → 2600ms): there are five things to read now
   and the old timing cut the name off mid-arrival. */
.camp-unlock-banner {
  position: fixed; top: 50%; left: 50%; transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
  text-align: center; z-index: 4200; pointer-events: none;
  display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; gap: 6px;
  animation: campUnlockIn 550ms cubic-bezier(.2,.9,.3,1.4) both,
             campUnlockOut 450ms ease-in 2600ms both;
}
/* Sits behind everything, centred on the logo. Zero-size box so it can
   never push the flex column around. */
.cub-burst {
  position: absolute; top: 96px; left: 50%; width: 0; height: 0;
  pointer-events: none;
}
.cub-rays {
  position: absolute; left: -190px; top: -190px; width: 380px; height: 380px;
  /* Hard-stop conic wedges, not a blurred gradient — at this size a soft
     one just reads as a dim smudge instead of light. */
  background: conic-gradient(from 0deg,
    rgba(77,255,212,0.30) 0deg 7deg, transparent 7deg 30deg,
    rgba(77,255,212,0.22) 30deg 36deg, transparent 36deg 60deg,
    rgba(255,209,102,0.26) 60deg 67deg, transparent 67deg 90deg,
    rgba(77,255,212,0.30) 90deg 97deg, transparent 97deg 120deg,
    rgba(255,209,102,0.20) 120deg 126deg, transparent 126deg 150deg,
    rgba(77,255,212,0.26) 150deg 157deg, transparent 157deg 180deg,
    rgba(77,255,212,0.30) 180deg 187deg, transparent 187deg 210deg,
    rgba(255,209,102,0.22) 210deg 216deg, transparent 216deg 240deg,
    rgba(77,255,212,0.26) 240deg 247deg, transparent 247deg 270deg,
    rgba(255,209,102,0.30) 270deg 277deg, transparent 277deg 300deg,
    rgba(77,255,212,0.22) 300deg 306deg, transparent 306deg 330deg,
    rgba(77,255,212,0.26) 330deg 337deg, transparent 337deg 360deg);
  /* Fade the rays toward their tips so they do not end in a hard disc. */
  -webkit-mask: radial-gradient(circle, #000 12%, rgba(0,0,0,0.55) 46%, transparent 72%);
  mask: radial-gradient(circle, #000 12%, rgba(0,0,0,0.55) 46%, transparent 72%);
  animation: cubRays 4.5s linear infinite, cubFadeIn 700ms ease-out both;
}
@keyframes cubRays { to { transform: rotate(360deg); } }
@keyframes cubFadeIn { from { opacity: 0; } to { opacity: 1; } }
.cub-ring {
  position: absolute; left: -60px; top: -60px; width: 120px; height: 120px;
  border-radius: 50%; border: 3px solid #4dffd4;
  animation: cubRing 1100ms cubic-bezier(.15,.75,.3,1) 120ms both;
}
.cub-ring2 { border-color: #ffd166; animation-delay: 380ms; }
@keyframes cubRing {
  0%   { transform: scale(0.25); opacity: 0.95; border-width: 5px; }
  100% { transform: scale(3.4);  opacity: 0;    border-width: 0.5px; }
}
.cub-sub {
  font-family: 'VT323', monospace; font-size: clamp(11px, 1.7vw, 15px);
  letter-spacing: 0.3em; color: #7fe8d4;
  text-shadow: 0 0 10px rgba(77,255,212,0.55), 0 2px 0 #000;
  animation: cubSub 500ms ease-out 1000ms both;
}
@keyframes cubSub {
  from { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(8px); letter-spacing: 0.1em; }
  to   { opacity: 0.9; transform: translateY(0); letter-spacing: 0.3em; }
}
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  .cub-rays, .cub-ring { animation: none; opacity: 0.35; }
  .cub-sub { animation: none; opacity: 0.9; }
}
.cub-tag {
  font-family: 'VT323', monospace; font-size: clamp(16px, 2.6vw, 22px);
  letter-spacing: 0.35em; color: #ffd166; text-shadow: 0 0 10px #ffd16699, 0 2px 0 #000;
}
.cub-icon {
  filter: drop-shadow(0 0 24px #4dffd4) drop-shadow(0 0 44px rgba(77,255,212,0.5));
  animation: campUnlockSwing 900ms ease-in-out 550ms both;
}
.cub-name {
  font-family: 'Cinzel', serif; font-weight: 900; letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  font-size: clamp(28px, 5.5vw, 46px); color: #fff;
  text-shadow: 0 0 20px #4dffd4, 0 0 44px rgba(77,255,212,0.5), 0 4px 0 #000;
}
@keyframes campUnlockIn {
  from { transform: translate(-50%, -50%) scale(0.4) rotate(-8deg); opacity: 0; }
  to   { transform: translate(-50%, -50%) scale(1) rotate(0deg); opacity: 1; }
}
@keyframes campUnlockOut { from { opacity: 1; } to { opacity: 0; } }
@keyframes campUnlockSwing {
  0%   { transform: rotate(0deg); }
  25%  { transform: rotate(-6deg); }
  50%  { transform: rotate(4deg); }
  75%  { transform: rotate(-2deg); }
  100% { transform: rotate(0deg); }
}

/* Camp arrival briefing — the one-time "why build the camp" text, replacing
   the retired combat tutorial (see App.js's startTutorialIfNeeded). A dead
   ship's status console rather than a storybook page: dark panel, a cold
   teal "still-alive" kicker against a warm "everything else is dead"
   orange, matching the --rune/--accent pair used everywhere else. */
.camp-brief-overlay {
  position: fixed; inset: 0; z-index: 2100;
  background: #020103d0; backdrop-filter: blur(6px);
  display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
  padding: 20px;
}
.camp-brief-card {
  position: relative;
  width: min(560px, 100%);
  padding: 22px 26px 20px;
  background:
    linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(16, 26, 30, 0.92), rgba(6, 10, 14, 0.96)), var(--bg-0);
  box-shadow:
    inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(77, 255, 212, 0.28),
    inset 0 0 0 2px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.8),
    0 24px 60px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.85),
    0 0 50px rgba(77, 255, 212, 0.14);
  clip-path: polygon(16px 0, calc(100% - 16px) 0, 100% 16px, 100% calc(100% - 16px), calc(100% - 16px) 100%, 16px 100%, 0 calc(100% - 16px), 0 16px);
  animation: campBriefIn 0.4s cubic-bezier(0.22,1,0.36,1) both;
}
@keyframes campBriefIn { from { transform: scale(0.92); opacity: 0; } to { transform: scale(1); opacity: 1; } }
.camp-brief-kicker {
  font-family: 'VT323', monospace; font-size: 15px; letter-spacing: 0.4em;
  color: var(--rune); text-shadow: 0 0 10px rgba(77,255,212,0.5);
}
.camp-brief-title {
  font-family: 'Cinzel', serif; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: 0.02em;
  font-size: clamp(20px, 4vw, 26px); color: var(--ink);
  margin: 4px 0 14px;
}
.camp-brief-body p {
  font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.55;
  color: var(--ink-dim); margin-bottom: 9px;
}
.camp-brief-body p:last-child { color: var(--ink); }
.camp-brief-actions {
  display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 14px;
  margin-top: 16px;
}
.camp-brief-skip {
  background: none; border: none; padding: 6px 2px;
  font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace; font-size: 12px;
  color: var(--ink-dim); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px;
  cursor: pointer; opacity: 0.75;
}
.camp-brief-skip:hover { opacity: 1; color: var(--ink); }
.camp-brief-go {
  font-family: 'VT323', monospace; font-size: 20px; letter-spacing: 0.14em;
  padding: 10px 22px; cursor: pointer;
  background: linear-gradient(180deg, #ff9a4d, #ff7a1a);
  border: 2px solid #ffb877; color: #1a0d02;
  box-shadow: 0 0 0 1px #000, 0 6px 0 #a4480a, 0 0 26px rgba(255,122,26,0.4);
  transition: transform 0.1s;
}
.camp-brief-go:hover { transform: translateY(-1px); }
.camp-brief-go:active { transform: translateY(2px); box-shadow: 0 0 0 1px #000, 0 3px 0 #a4480a; }
@media (max-width: 480px) {
  .camp-brief-actions { flex-direction: column-reverse; align-items: stretch; }
  .camp-brief-go { width: 100%; }
  .camp-brief-skip { text-align: center; }
}
/* Weapon-fork screen: exactly 4 octagon cards, 2x2 (2 side by side, 2 below). */
.card-row-fork { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 240px); gap: 22px; justify-content: center; }
.card-fork { --rar: #b362ff; --glow: 26px; }
.card-fork.r-epic { animation: cardIn 280ms cubic-bezier(.2,.9,.3,1.4) both, forkCardPulse 900ms ease-in-out 280ms infinite alternate; }
@keyframes forkCardPulse { from { box-shadow: var(--pixel-edge), 0 12px 0 #000, 0 0 0 2px #b362ff, 0 0 24px #b362ff; } to { box-shadow: var(--pixel-edge), 0 12px 0 #000, 0 0 0 2px #b362ff, 0 0 48px #b362ff, 0 0 70px rgba(179,98,255,0.4); } }
@media (max-width: 720px) {
  .card-row-fork { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 10px; }
}
.card {
  width: 240px; min-height: 320px;
  flex: 0 1 240px;
  background: linear-gradient(180deg, #1a1226 0%, #0a0612 100%);
  background-color: var(--rar-bg, transparent);
  border: 2px solid #000;
  border-left: 3px solid var(--rar, #333);
  --glow: 8px;
  box-shadow: var(--pixel-edge), 0 12px 0 #000, 0 0 0 2px var(--rar), 0 0 var(--glow) var(--rar);
  padding: 18px 16px;
  cursor: pointer;
  display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; gap: 10px;
  transition: transform 120ms, box-shadow 120ms;
  position: relative;
  overflow: hidden;
  animation: cardIn 280ms cubic-bezier(.2,.9,.3,1.4) both;
  /* Unique per-rarity silhouette, not just a plain rectangle — the shape
     itself gets more elaborate as rarity climbs (see per-tier clip-path
     overrides below). */
  clip-path: polygon(10px 0, 100% 0, 100% calc(100% - 10px), calc(100% - 10px) 100%, 0 100%, 0 10px);
}
.card:hover {
  transform: translateY(-8px) rotateX(-4deg) scale(1.02);
  box-shadow: var(--pixel-edge), 0 18px 0 #000, 0 0 40px var(--rar);
}
.card:active { transform: translateY(-2px) scale(0.985); }

/* Rarity aura — a soft wash of the rarity colour rising through the card,
   breathing on its own timer. This is what makes a legendary read as
   legendary from across the screen before you have read a word of it.
   Kept INSIDE the card on purpose: .card is overflow:hidden for the shine
   sweep, so anything bleeding past the edge would simply be clipped. */
.card::after {
  content: '';
  position: absolute;
  inset: 0;
  pointer-events: none;
  background: radial-gradient(ellipse 120% 70% at 50% 22%, var(--rar) 0%, transparent 70%);
  opacity: var(--aura, 0.10);
  mix-blend-mode: screen;
  animation: cardAura 2.6s ease-in-out infinite;
}
@keyframes cardAura {
  0%, 100% { opacity: calc(var(--aura, 0.10) * 0.55); }
  50%      { opacity: var(--aura, 0.10); }
}
/* Content sits above the aura — an absolutely positioned ::after paints
   after its siblings, so at mythical strength it would otherwise wash the
   name and description out. */
.card-portrait, .card-type-badge, .card-lvl-dots, .card-name, .card-desc {
  position: relative; z-index: 2;
}
/* These two are already absolutely positioned — only lift them, don't
   re-declare position or they jump out of their corners. */
.card-tag, .card-evo-badge { z-index: 2; }
.card.r-common    { --aura: 0.05; }
.card.r-uncommon  { --aura: 0.14; }
.card.r-rare      { --aura: 0.22; }
.card.r-epic      { --aura: 0.32; }
.card.r-legendary { --aura: 0.42; }
.card.r-mythical  { --aura: 0.55; }
/* Pick "out" animation — the chosen card punches up and glows hard while
   the rest fade/slide away, instead of the whole modal just vanishing. */
.card-chosen {
  animation: cardChosen 480ms cubic-bezier(.2,.9,.2,1) both;
  z-index: 5;
}
.card-rejected {
  animation: cardRejected 380ms ease-in both;
  pointer-events: none;
}
@keyframes cardChosen {
  0% { transform: scale(1); }
  35% { transform: scale(1.14) translateY(-10px); box-shadow: var(--pixel-edge), 0 18px 0 #000, 0 0 60px var(--rar); }
  100% { transform: scale(1.22) translateY(-16px); opacity: 0; box-shadow: var(--pixel-edge), 0 18px 0 #000, 0 0 90px var(--rar); }
}
@keyframes cardRejected {
  0% { transform: scale(1); opacity: 1; }
  100% { transform: scale(0.85) translateY(14px); opacity: 0; }
}
.card.r-common    { --rar: #9a8fa6; --glow: 6px;  background: linear-gradient(180deg, #16121f 0%, #0a0612 100%); }
.card.r-uncommon  { --rar: #4dff91; --glow: 12px; background: linear-gradient(180deg, #0d1f14 0%, #0a0612 100%); clip-path: polygon(14px 0, 100% 0, 100% calc(100% - 14px), calc(100% - 14px) 100%, 0 100%, 0 14px); }
.card.r-rare      { --rar: #4dc4ff; --glow: 18px; background: linear-gradient(180deg, #0d1820 0%, #0a0612 100%); clip-path: polygon(18px 0, calc(100% - 18px) 0, 100% 18px, 100% 100%, calc(100% - 18px) 100%, 0 100%, 0 18px); }
.card.r-epic      { --rar: #b362ff; --glow: 24px; background: linear-gradient(180deg, #180d20 0%, #0a0612 100%); clip-path: polygon(20px 0, calc(100% - 20px) 0, 100% 20px, 100% calc(100% - 20px), calc(100% - 20px) 100%, 20px 100%, 0 calc(100% - 20px), 0 20px); }
.card.r-legendary { --rar: #ff7a1a; --glow: 30px; background: linear-gradient(180deg, #200f07 0%, #0a0612 100%); clip-path: polygon(24px 0, calc(100% - 24px) 0, 100% 24px, 100% calc(100% - 24px), calc(100% - 24px) 100%, 24px 100%, 0 calc(100% - 24px), 0 24px); }
.card.r-mythical  { --rar: #ff3146; --glow: 34px; background: linear-gradient(180deg, #200810 0%, #0a0612 100%); clip-path: polygon(50% 0, 82% 10px, 100% 28px, 100% calc(100% - 28px), 82% calc(100% - 10px), 50% 100%, 18% calc(100% - 10px), 0 calc(100% - 28px), 0 28px, 18% 10px); animation: cardIn 280ms cubic-bezier(.2,.9,.3,1.4) both, mythCardPulse 700ms ease-in-out 280ms infinite alternate; }
@keyframes mythCardPulse { from { box-shadow: var(--pixel-edge), 0 12px 0 #000, 0 0 0 2px #ff3146, 0 0 20px #ff3146; } to { box-shadow: var(--pixel-edge), 0 12px 0 #000, 0 0 0 2px #ff3146, 0 0 44px #ff3146, 0 0 64px rgba(255,49,70,0.35); } }
.card-rarity {
  font-family: 'VT323', monospace;
  letter-spacing: 0.3em;
  font-size: 14px;
  color: var(--rar);
}
/* Icon "logo holder" — a faceted medallion frame behind the card's emoji
   icon, tinted by rarity, instead of the icon floating bare on the card. */
.card-portrait {
  width: 76px; height: 76px;
  border-radius: 50%;
  display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
  background: radial-gradient(circle at 50% 40%, color-mix(in srgb, var(--rar) 35%, #0a0612) 0%, #0a0612 78%);
  box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 2px var(--rar), inset 0 0 16px #000, 0 0 14px var(--rar);
  position: relative;
}
.card-portrait::before {
  content: '';
  position: absolute; inset: -6px;
  border-radius: 50%;
  border: 1px dashed color-mix(in srgb, var(--rar) 55%, transparent);
  animation: cardPortraitSpin 9s linear infinite;
}
@keyframes cardPortraitSpin { to { transform: rotate(360deg); } }
.card-icon {
  font-size: 40px;
  filter: drop-shadow(0 0 10px var(--rar));
}
/* Drawn weapon glyph in the medallion. Tilted very slightly and lifted off
   the plate so the portrait reads as a relief rather than a flat sticker. */
.card-glyph {
  filter: drop-shadow(0 2px 3px rgba(0,0,0,0.8)) drop-shadow(0 0 9px var(--rar));
  transform: rotate(-8deg);
}
.game-icon { display: block; }
/* Weapon picker + header in the smith */
.forge-wch .game-icon { margin: 0 auto 2px; filter: drop-shadow(0 1px 3px rgba(0,0,0,0.8)); }
.forge-wch.sel .game-icon { filter: drop-shadow(0 0 8px currentColor) drop-shadow(0 1px 3px #000); }
.forge-name { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; }
.card-name { font-family: 'Cinzel', serif; font-weight: 800; font-size: 18px; color: var(--ink); text-align: center; }
.card-desc { font-family: 'VT323', monospace; font-size: 18px; color: var(--ink-dim); text-align: center; line-height: 1.2; }
.card-desc b { color: var(--rar); font-weight: 700; }
/* Signed stat deltas read at a glance: gains green, losses red. Unsigned
   quantities keep the rarity tint so "3 projectiles" isn't mistaken for a
   change of +3. */
.card-desc b.sv-up {
  color: #6dff9e;
  text-shadow: 0 0 8px rgba(109,255,158,0.55);
}
.card-desc b.sv-down {
  color: #ff6a7a;
  text-shadow: 0 0 8px rgba(255,106,122,0.55);
}
.card-tag {
  position: absolute; top: -1px; left: -1px;
  background: var(--rar); color: #000;
  font-family: 'VT323', monospace; font-size: 12px;
  padding: 2px 8px; letter-spacing: 0.2em;
}
/* Type badge (weapon-new / upgrade / evolve / passive / stat) — icon+label
   pill instead of bare text, sits under the portrait. */
.card-type-badge {
  display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 5px;
  font-family: 'VT323', monospace; font-size: 13px; letter-spacing: 0.18em;
  color: var(--rar);
  background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--rar) 14%, #000);
  border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--rar) 60%, #000);
  padding: 2px 10px;
  border-radius: 3px;
}
/* Evolution badge — distinct pulsing gold ribbon, only on evolve picks. */
.card-evo-badge {
  position: absolute; top: 8px; right: 8px;
  font-family: 'VT323', monospace; font-size: 12px; letter-spacing: 0.15em;
  color: #0a0612; background: linear-gradient(135deg, #ffe066, #ff9900);
  padding: 2px 8px; border-radius: 2px;
  box-shadow: 0 0 10px #ff9900cc;
  animation: cardEvoPulse 900ms ease-in-out infinite alternate;
}
@keyframes cardEvoPulse { from { box-shadow: 0 0 8px #ff9900aa; } to { box-shadow: 0 0 18px #ffcc44ee; } }
/* Level pips — filled dots for the weapon's current level, one hollow dot
   glowing for the level this pick would reach. */
.card-lvl-dots { display: flex; gap: 4px; align-items: center; }
.card-lvl-dot {
  width: 7px; height: 7px; border-radius: 50%;
  background: #221a2c; box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px #000;
}
.card-lvl-dot.filled { background: var(--rar); box-shadow: 0 0 5px var(--rar); }
.card-lvl-dot.next { background: transparent; box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 2px var(--rar), 0 0 8px var(--rar); animation: cardEvoPulse 700ms ease-in-out infinite alternate; }
.card-lvl-text { font-family: 'VT323', monospace; font-size: 12px; color: var(--ink-dim); letter-spacing: 0.1em; }

/* GAME OVER */
.gameover {
  width: min(640px, 92vw);
  padding: 38px 42px;
  background: linear-gradient(180deg, #2a0f0f 0%, #0a0612 100%);
  border: 2px solid #000;
  box-shadow: 0 0 0 2px #b51d2888, 0 30px 80px #000c;
  text-align: center;
}
.gameover h1 {
  font-size: 64px;
  background: linear-gradient(180deg, #ff3146, #b51d28);
  -webkit-background-clip: text; background-clip: text; color: transparent;
  margin-bottom: 8px;
}
.gameover .stats {
  display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 10px 24px;
  margin: 22px 0;
  font-family: 'VT323', monospace;
  font-size: 20px;
}
.gameover .stat-row { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; padding: 6px 10px; background: #00000044; border-left: 2px solid var(--accent); }
.gameover .stat-row span:first-child { color: var(--ink-dim); }
.gameover .stat-row span:last-child { color: var(--accent-2); }

/* CAMP */
.camp {
  width: min(1100px, 100%);
  min-height: min(86vh, 800px);
  display: flex;
  background: linear-gradient(180deg, #0e1a26 0%, #07060c 100%);
  border: 2px solid #000;
  box-shadow: 0 0 0 2px #4dc4ff44, 0 30px 80px #000c;
  position: relative;
}
.camp::before {
  content: '';
  position: absolute; inset: 0;
  background:
    radial-gradient(circle at 30% 60%, #ff7a1a22 0%, transparent 30%),
    radial-gradient(circle at 70% 40%, #4dc4ff22 0%, transparent 30%);
  pointer-events: none;
}
.camp-sidebar {
  width: 240px;
  background: #00000066;
  border-right: 2px solid #000;
  display: flex; flex-direction: column;
  z-index: 1;
  overflow: hidden;
}
.camp-tabs-scroll {
  flex: 1;
  display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 6px;
  padding: 14px 14px 8px 14px;
  overflow-y: auto;
  overflow-x: hidden;
  scroll-behavior: smooth;
}
.camp-profile-bar {
  display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px;
  padding: 12px 16px;
  border-bottom: 1px solid #ffffff22;
  background: linear-gradient(180deg, #1a1228, #0e0816);
  flex-shrink: 0;
}
/* Frames the entire bar (avatar+name+rank+currencies) as one cohesive
   plaque instead of a bare strip — a thin lit border + soft inner glow. */
.camp-profile-bar-framed {
  border: 1px solid var(--rune, #4dffd4aa);
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rune, #4dffd4aa);
  box-shadow: 0 0 0 1px #00000080, inset 0 0 22px rgba(77,255,212,0.06), 0 4px 14px rgba(0,0,0,0.5);
  position: relative;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
}
.camp-profile-id { cursor: pointer; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; }
/* Avatar always gets a decorative ring, even with no cosmetic frame
   unlocked yet — the unlocked PROFILE_FRAMES css/glow layers on top via
   the --frame-css custom property + inline boxShadow. */
.camp-avatar-frame {
  width: 44px; height: 44px; border-radius: 50%;
  display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
  position: relative;
  border: var(--frame-css, none);
  background: radial-gradient(circle at 50% 35%, #23182f 0%, #0a0612 75%);
}
.camp-avatar-frame::before {
  content: ''; position: absolute; inset: -3px; border-radius: 50%;
  border: 1.5px solid rgba(77,255,212,0.5);
  box-shadow: 0 0 8px rgba(77,255,212,0.35);
  pointer-events: none;
}
.camp-avatar-icon { font-size: 24px; position: relative; z-index: 1; }
/* Currencies laid out side by side as small pill chips, wraps on narrow
   screens instead of stacking one-per-line. */
/* One row, never wrapping — it scrolls sideways instead, so adding a
   currency can't silently make the banner taller. */
.camp-currency-row {
  flex-basis: 100%;
  display: flex; align-items: center; flex-wrap: nowrap; gap: 4px;
  font-family: 'VT323', monospace; font-size: 12px; color: var(--ink-dim);
  max-width: 100%;
  overflow-x: auto;
  scrollbar-width: none;
  padding-bottom: 1px;
}
.camp-currency-row::-webkit-scrollbar { display: none; }
/* Shelf treatment: each chip is a lit recess rather than a flat pill. */
.camp-currency-chip {
  background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(255,255,255,0.09) 0%, rgba(0,0,0,0.35) 100%);
  border: 1px solid #ffffff20;
  border-radius: 4px;
  padding: 2px 7px; white-space: nowrap; flex: 0 0 auto;
  box-shadow: inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255,255,255,0.14), inset 0 -2px 4px rgba(0,0,0,0.45), 0 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,0.5);
}

/* Rolling counters (see CountUp in Camp.jsx). Timmy: a currency updating
   should "bli lite större å lysa till" (get a bit bigger and light up) —
   color+arrow alone read as a state change but not really as a moment. The
   pop is on the number itself (transform-origin center) so it doesn't
   shove neighboring chips in the row. */
.countup { position: relative; display: inline-block; transition: color 0.2s, text-shadow 0.2s; }
.countup.is-up   { color: #6dff9e; text-shadow: 0 0 9px rgba(109,255,158,0.6); animation: countPop 0.5s cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.8, 0.3, 1.4); }
.countup.is-down { color: #ff6a7a; text-shadow: 0 0 9px rgba(255,106,122,0.6); animation: countPop 0.5s cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.8, 0.3, 1.4); }
@keyframes countPop {
  0%   { transform: scale(1); }
  35%  { transform: scale(1.28); }
  100% { transform: scale(1); }
}
.countup-arrow {
  font-style: normal;
  font-size: 0.62em;
  margin-left: 2px;
  vertical-align: 0.15em;
  animation: countArrow 0.6s ease-out infinite;
}
@keyframes countArrow {
  0%, 100% { opacity: 0.45; transform: translateY(0); }
  50%      { opacity: 1; transform: translateY(-2px); }
}

/* Attribute toggle — sits under the avatar on the left, per the request
   that only the left side of the banner drops down. */
.camp-attr-toggle {
  flex-basis: 100%;
  display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px;
  align-self: flex-start;
  width: max-content;
  font-family: 'VT323', monospace; font-size: 13px; letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  color: #c890ff;
  background: #c890ff0f; border: 1px solid #c890ff44; border-radius: 4px;
  padding: 3px 10px;
  cursor: pointer;
  transition: background 0.14s, border-color 0.14s;
}
.camp-attr-toggle:hover { background: #c890ff1f; border-color: #c890ff88; }
.camp-attr-toggle.open { background: #c890ff22; border-color: #c890ffaa; }
.camp-attr-caret { font-size: 10px; opacity: 0.8; }

/* Rendered via a React portal straight into document.body (see Camp.jsx) —
   NOT a descendant of .camp-sidebar in the DOM. It has to be: .camp-sidebar
   is a flex item with its own z-index, which makes it a stacking context,
   and .camp-main (a later sibling, same z-index) painted over the whole
   thing regardless of what z-index this panel used, because that contest
   never reached this element in the first place. position:fixed alone does
   NOT escape an ancestor's stacking context, only its layout/overflow —
   that's why the previous position:fixed-only attempt still failed. */
.camp-attr-panel {
  z-index: 60;
  overflow-y: auto;
  background: linear-gradient(180deg, #140c22 0%, #0a0612 100%);
  border: 1px solid #c890ff66;
  box-shadow: 0 14px 34px rgba(0,0,0,0.75), 0 0 24px rgba(200,144,255,0.18), inset 0 0 18px rgba(200,144,255,0.07);
  padding: 10px;
  text-align: left;
  animation: attrPanelIn 180ms ease-out both;
}
@keyframes attrPanelIn {
  from { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(-6px); }
  to   { opacity: 1; transform: none; }
}
.camp-tab-divider {
  height: 1px; background: #ffffff14; margin: 2px 0;
}
.camp-sidebar h2 {
  font-size: 18px; color: var(--accent-2); letter-spacing: 0.2em;
  margin-bottom: 16px;
}
.camp-tab {
  text-align: left; padding: 14px 18px; font-size: 14px;
  background: #0e0816; border: 2px solid #000;
  box-shadow: var(--pixel-edge);
  position: relative; overflow: hidden;
  transition: transform 80ms, box-shadow 80ms, background 140ms;
}
.camp-tab:hover:not(.active):not(.locked) {
  background: #1a1228;
  transform: translateX(3px);
  box-shadow: var(--pixel-edge), 2px 0 0 #ff7a1a55;
}
/* Camp starts locked and opens panel by panel as the story's first three
   nodes clear (see campaign.js's campUnlockStage) — this is the same
   dimmed/no-hover treatment the Card Shop's EVOLUTIONS section already
   used for "unlock via Skill Tree", kept consistent rather than inventing
   a second locked-button language. */
.camp-tab.locked {
  opacity: 0.4;
  cursor: not-allowed;
  filter: grayscale(0.6);
}
.camp-tab.locked:hover { transform: none; }
.camp-tab.active {
  color: var(--accent);
  background: linear-gradient(90deg, #1c0e2a, #0e0816);
  box-shadow: var(--pixel-edge), 0 0 0 2px #ff7a1a, 4px 0 0 #ff7a1a;
}
.camp-main {
  flex: 1;
  padding: 24px 28px 0 28px;
  z-index: 1;
  display: flex; flex-direction: column;
  min-height: 100%;
}
.camp-header {
  display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-end;
  margin-bottom: 18px;
  border-bottom: 1px dashed #ffffff22;
  padding-bottom: 12px;
}
.camp-header h1 { font-size: 22px; color: var(--ink); text-align: center; }
.camp-currency {
  display: flex; gap: 18px;
  font-family: 'VT323', monospace; font-size: 22px;
}
.camp-currency .gold { color: var(--accent-2); }
.camp-currency .essence { color: var(--rune); }
.upgrade-grid {
  display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(min(220px, 100%), 1fr));
  gap: 14px;
}
.upgrade-card {
  background: linear-gradient(180deg, #15101e, #0a0612);
  border: 2px solid #000;
  box-shadow: var(--pixel-edge);
  padding: 14px;
  display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px;
  position: relative;
}
.upgrade-card .name { font-family: 'Cinzel', serif; font-weight: 800; color: var(--ink); font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: 0.08em; }
.upgrade-card .desc { font-family: 'VT323', monospace; font-size: 17px; color: var(--ink-dim); min-height: 40px; }
.upgrade-card .lvl { font-family: 'VT323', monospace; color: var(--rune); font-size: 16px; letter-spacing: 0.2em; }
.upgrade-card .pips { display: flex; gap: 3px; margin: 4px 0; }
.upgrade-card .pip { width: 14px; height: 6px; background: #00000099; border: 1px solid #000; }
.upgrade-card .pip.on { background: var(--accent); box-shadow: 0 0 6px #ff7a1a; }
.upgrade-card button { padding: 8px 10px; font-size: 12px; }
.upgrade-card.maxed { opacity: 0.7; }
.upgrade-card.maxed .name { color: var(--accent-2); }

.camp-actions {
  position: sticky; bottom: 0;
  align-self: flex-end;
  display: flex; gap: 10px;
  z-index: 2;
  padding: 14px 16px;
  background: linear-gradient(180deg, transparent, #07060ce6 50%);
  width: 100%;
  justify-content: flex-end;
  margin-top: auto;
}

/* Meta-upgrade purchase "cha-ching" — anchored right above the button that
   was clicked instead of a generic banner, floats up and fades, with a
   brief whole-panel shake (.camp-shake) for real weight on the purchase. */
@keyframes campShakeKf {
  0%, 100% { transform: translate(0, 0); }
  20% { transform: translate(-3px, 2px); }
  40% { transform: translate(3px, -2px); }
  60% { transform: translate(-2px, -1px); }
  80% { transform: translate(2px, 1px); }
}
.camp-shake { animation: campShakeKf 260ms ease-in-out; }
@keyframes metaBurstFloat {
  0%   { opacity: 0; transform: translate(-50%, 0) scale(0.7); }
  15%  { opacity: 1; transform: translate(-50%, -6px) scale(1.15); }
  30%  { transform: translate(-50%, -14px) scale(1); }
  100% { opacity: 0; transform: translate(-50%, -70px) scale(1); }
}
.meta-burst {
  position: fixed; z-index: 9999; pointer-events: none;
  display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; gap: 2px;
  animation: metaBurstFloat 1100ms ease-out both;
}
/* Was `.meta-burst-icon { font-size: 26px }` showing metaBurst.icon as raw
   TEXT — fine while that field held a single emoji glyph, but it now holds
   a GameIcon key (see no-emoji-rule), and an 8-13 character identifier like
   "moveMult" at 26px text overflowed the whole card. Icon is a fixed-size
   GameIcon now, so this only sizes its wrapper; the name below is the thing
   Timmy actually wants prominent on a purchase, so it gets the weight the
   icon used to have by accident. */
.meta-burst-icon { filter: drop-shadow(0 0 10px #ffd166); }
.meta-burst-name {
  font-family: 'VT323', monospace; font-size: 22px; font-weight: 700;
  color: #ffe9a8; text-shadow: 0 0 10px #ffd16699; white-space: nowrap;
  letter-spacing: 0.04em;
}
.meta-burst-gain {
  font-family: 'VT323', monospace; font-size: 17px; color: #4dff91;
  text-shadow: 0 0 8px #4dff9199; white-space: nowrap;
}

.toast {
  position: fixed; top: 20px; left: 50%; transform: translateX(-50%);
  padding: 10px 18px;
  background: #000c;
  border: 2px solid var(--accent);
  color: var(--accent-2);
  font-family: 'VT323', monospace; letter-spacing: 0.2em;
  z-index: 50;
  animation: cardIn 200ms;
}

/* PAUSE */
.pause-overlay {
  position: fixed; inset: 0;
  background: #000c;
  display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
  z-index: 9;
  backdrop-filter: blur(4px);
}
.pause-box {
  background: linear-gradient(180deg, #1a2e34 0%, #0a1519 100%);
  border: 2px solid #000;
  box-shadow:
    inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(140, 220, 228, 0.24),
    0 0 0 2px #4dffd444,
    0 20px 60px #000;
  padding: 36px 44px;
  text-align: center;
  display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 14px;
}
.pause-box h2 { font-size: 32px; color: #cfe6ec; letter-spacing: 0.3em; }
.pause-sheet {
  text-align: left;
  min-width: min(420px, 78vw);
  padding: 10px 4px 4px;
  border-top: 1px solid rgba(140, 220, 228, 0.18);
}
.pause-kv {
  font-family: 'VT323', monospace;
  font-size: 16px;
  letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  color: #9fb3c8;
  margin-bottom: 8px;
}
.pause-kv b { color: #e9f4ff; }
.pause-hp {
  height: 8px;
  background: #071018;
  border: 1px solid #ffffff18;
  margin-bottom: 10px;
  overflow: hidden;
}
.pause-hp i {
  display: block;
  height: 100%;
  background: linear-gradient(90deg, #4dffd4, #1a8a7a);
}
.pause-loadout {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  gap: 6px;
  margin-bottom: 6px;
}
.pause-w {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 4px;
  font-family: 'VT323', monospace;
  font-size: 13px;
  letter-spacing: 0.06em;
  color: #cfe6ff;
  background: #ffffff0c;
  border: 1px solid #ffffff18;
  padding: 4px 8px;
}
.pause-passives {
  font-family: 'VT323', monospace;
  font-size: 12px;
  color: #8aa0b4;
  letter-spacing: 0.04em;
}
.pause-box button {
  font-family: 'VT323', monospace;
  letter-spacing: 0.12em;
  padding: 10px 14px;
  cursor: pointer;
}

/* HELP / CONTROLS */
.help {
  position: absolute; top: 14px; right: 14px;
  font-family: 'VT323', monospace;
  color: var(--ink-dim);
  font-size: 14px;
  text-align: right;
  pointer-events: none;
  z-index: 3;
  text-shadow: 0 1px 0 #000;
}
.help b { color: var(--accent-2); }

/* loading screen */
.boot {
  position: fixed; inset: 0;
  display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
  flex-direction: column; gap: 16px;
  background: #07060c;
  z-index: 100;
  font-family: 'VT323', monospace;
  color: var(--rune);
  letter-spacing: 0.4em;
}
.boot-spin {
  width: 60px; height: 60px;
  border: 3px solid #4dffd433;
  border-top-color: var(--rune);
  border-radius: 50%;
  animation: spin 0.8s linear infinite;
}
@keyframes spin { to { transform: rotate(360deg); } }

@media (max-width: 720px) {
  .menu { padding: 24px; }
  .card-row { gap: 10px; }
  .card { width: 46%; min-width: 140px; min-height: 220px; padding: 12px 8px; flex: 1 1 46%; }
  .card-icon { font-size: 36px !important; }
  .card-name { font-size: 13px !important; }
  .card-desc { font-size: 14px !important; }
  .hud-stats { font-size: 14px; gap: 10px; }
  .camp { flex-direction: column; min-height: auto; }
  .camp-sidebar {
    width: 100%; flex-direction: column;
    border-right: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #000;
    max-height: 220px;
  }
  .camp-tabs-scroll {
    flex-direction: row; flex-wrap: nowrap;
    overflow-x: auto; overflow-y: hidden;
    padding: 10px 12px 6px 12px;
    gap: 6px;
    /* Right-fade hint: more content scrollable */
    -webkit-mask-image: linear-gradient(to right, black 85%, transparent 100%);
    mask-image: linear-gradient(to right, black 85%, transparent 100%);
  }
  .camp-tabs-scroll .camp-tab { flex-shrink: 0; padding: 8px 10px; font-size: 11px; }
  .camp-tabs-scroll .camp-tab-divider { width: 1px; height: auto; min-height: 32px; margin: 0 2px; }
  .camp-profile-bar { padding: 6px 12px; font-size: 11px; }
  .camp-main { padding: 16px 14px 110px 14px; }
  /* minmax(0, ...) not 1fr: a bare 1fr floors the track at the item's
     min-content width, which the 20-pip meta upgrades push past the screen. */
  .upgrade-grid { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 8px; }
  .upgrade-card { padding: 10px; }
  .upgrade-card .name { font-size: 12px; }
  .upgrade-card .desc { font-size: 14px; min-height: 30px; }
  .welcome-grid { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }
  /* ONE ROW OF SEVEN, on the phone too — that is what the reference shows.
     This used to drop to 4 columns, which with the old 14 cells wrapped into
     four rows ending in a ragged two-cell tail: the "ihoptryckt" Timmy
     reported. Seven cells across 393px would be ~45px each and unreadable, so
     the row scrolls horizontally instead of crushing, and each cell keeps a
     legible floor. The current day is scrolled into view by the browser
     because it is the only focusable-looking thing... it is not, so if that
     ever matters, scroll it in explicitly. */
  .daily-row {
    display: flex;
    gap: 6px;
    overflow-x: auto;
    overscroll-behavior-x: contain;
    scroll-snap-type: x proximity;
    -webkit-overflow-scrolling: touch;
    padding-bottom: 4px;
  }
  .daily-cell {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    min-width: 72px;
    scroll-snap-align: center;
  }
  .profile-card { padding: 12px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .profile-curr { flex-direction: row; gap: 10px; font-size: 16px; }
  .hud-bottom { flex-direction: column; gap: 8px; align-items: stretch; }
  .hud-hp { width: 100%; }
  .help { display: none; }
  .skilltree-panel, .forge-panel, .shop-panel { padding: 12px; }
  .st-grid { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }
  .chest-row { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1fr); }
  .levelup-mega { font-size: 20px; letter-spacing: 0.3em; }
  .levelup-sub { font-size: 14px; letter-spacing: 0.15em; }
  .weapon-strip { bottom: 130px; transform: translateX(-50%) scale(0.85); }
}

@media (max-width: 420px) {
  .upgrade-grid { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }
  .chest-row { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }
  .card { width: 100%; flex: 1 1 100%; }
}

/* ============== EXTENDED UI ============== */

